WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.550
My name is Julie. I am the
director at Luxe Bag Spa.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.916
Here at Luxe Bag Spa,

00:00:12.916 --> 00:00:15.849
we restore luxury designer handbags.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:18.930
I'm going to show you how
we are going to restore

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.600
this very loved Chanel handbag.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.880
This is a Chanel classic flap,

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.000
and it's about 12 to 15 years old.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.980
A bag like this, the state that it's in,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.960
it would be about $1,500.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.250
After the restoration,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.270
it could go to about 5,000 or 6,000 USD.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.730
The bag definitely needs
a really good clean.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.530
We're going to do a full coloration

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.420
as well as take the strap apart

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.238
and make sure we're polishing
all of the hardware.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.110
This bag looks to have many years

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.260
of dirt and grime buildup on it.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.110
First, we're going to go ahead

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:59.418
and clean the exterior of the bag

00:00:59.418 --> 00:01:02.280
just with a gentle, mild leather cleaner

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.350
using a horsehair brush.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.380
This really helps get into the leather

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.040
and the cracks of where the stitching is.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.101
So we're able to really get a deep clean

00:01:14.101 --> 00:01:17.163
without hurting any of
the exterior leather.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.898
I'm going to go in now

00:01:20.898 --> 00:01:23.289
with our leather-moisturizing cream.

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:24.855
I want to use this actually

00:01:24.855 --> 00:01:26.946
before I start pigmenting the bag,

00:01:26.946 --> 00:01:29.760
because I don't want the bag to crack.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.520
So I will just let this
sit on for a little bit.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:34.590
It has avocado oil in it,

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.863
so it will bring back a lot
of its original moisture.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.690
Now we've unraveled the entire chain,

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.490
and the reason that we're doing this is

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.460
because we want to polish
the hardware separately

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.876
from it being attached

00:01:51.876 --> 00:01:54.540
to the leather of the chain.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.231
We're going to go in

00:01:56.231 --> 00:01:58.355
with the same leather-cleaning solution

00:01:58.355 --> 00:02:00.900
that we did for the exterior of the bag,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.608
and we're going to also use

00:02:02.608 --> 00:02:04.574
the gentle horsehair brush.

00:02:09.784 --> 00:02:11.160
Now that we've finished cleaning,

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.970
I'm going to go in with a
acetone-based leather primer.

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.412
So, we want to take off

00:02:16.412 --> 00:02:19.595
even more pigment if we are able to,

00:02:19.595 --> 00:02:22.140
just to make sure that the bag is prepped

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:24.348
and ready for the coloration.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.605
Looking in the interior, you can see that

00:02:29.605 --> 00:02:32.959
there is some of the
original color still in here.

00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:34.320
So this is actually what we're going

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.393
to be color-matching in the bag.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.840
I'm going to go in with
a small angled brush,

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.265
just so I have more control

00:02:41.265 --> 00:02:43.590
over concealing these areas.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.615
I like to think of the bags

00:02:45.615 --> 00:02:47.314
as how you would do your makeup.

00:02:47.314 --> 00:02:49.890
You want to conceal the darker spots first

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.070
before applying the rest of the pigment.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.590
This just makes it more
cohesive throughout

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:59.913
and makes the bag look like
it did as the original.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.170
I'm switching now to a larger paintbrush

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.320
when we're doing the
full exterior coloration.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.811
This just helps me cover

00:03:11.811 --> 00:03:13.770
more surface area of the bag

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.920
and really get into those grooves.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.230
I am painting this bag by hand

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.873
because I find I have a lot more control.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:27.180
I'm going to apply
filler to this area here

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.995
to make it smooth on this interior flap.

00:03:32.141 --> 00:03:34.200
After the filler is completely dry,

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.490
we want to go in with a sander.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:39.030
We just want to make sure
that everything is level

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.445
and just looks natural on this flap.

00:03:44.747 --> 00:03:46.280
As you can see here,

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.813
I have left the panel surrounding the CC

00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:51.000
without any pigment,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.070
and you can already see
the color difference

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.060
between the two.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.385
But the reason we're doing this is because

00:03:56.385 --> 00:04:00.540
we don't want the silver polish to destroy

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.060
or deteriorate any of the pigment

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.560
that we're going to put on now,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:07.385
since it is quite a harsh chemical.

00:04:07.385 --> 00:04:10.800
So I go into all the
hardware with a Q-tip,

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.350
just dipping it into the silver polish

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.230
and rubbing away any tarnish or dirt

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.273
that has collected over the years.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:22.500
I'm going in with an angled brush

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.350
that I also used for concealing this bag.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.840
I just want to be a
little bit more precise

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.720
with painting around the CC.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.900
And if I get any pigment on the CC,

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.910
it doesn't really matter.

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.970
I'm able to take a Q-tip
and wipe that right off.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.766
But I try and keep it
as clean as possible.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.800
Now I'm going to go in
with the second layer,

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.900
and I'm doing this a little bit thinner

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:50.441
than the one prior.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:57.870
Now we're going to look
at doing coloration

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.280
on the strap here.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.490
We're going to go in and
conceal the dark marks,

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:06.300
just like we did on the
exterior of the full bag,

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:10.748
and then go in and paint
the entirety of the strap.

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:18.948
Even though we did polish

00:05:18.948 --> 00:05:20.460
the entirety of this chain,

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.943
there is a few spots

00:05:21.943 --> 00:05:24.120
that we want to re-silver-plate.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.395
For these spots here,

00:05:25.395 --> 00:05:28.486
we will use our re-silver-plating tool,

00:05:28.486 --> 00:05:30.660
which we dip into a solution,

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:34.018
and with electromagnets it actually

00:05:34.018 --> 00:05:37.234
puts silver back onto
where it's scratched off

00:05:37.234 --> 00:05:39.788
or tarnished off over time.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.750
Now that the strap is completely dry,

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.270
we're going to weave it back together.

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:50.310
When doing this, we want to make sure

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:52.620
that the strap is completely straight.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.178
And if it isn't,

00:05:54.178 --> 00:05:57.270
then your Chanel bag
is going to be turning

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.340
in a whole bunch of different directions,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.731
so this is a really important step.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.706
Using the same leather solution

00:06:06.706 --> 00:06:08.256
that we did on the exterior,

00:06:08.256 --> 00:06:10.830
I'm going to go in with a horsehair brush

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.620
and clean the inside here.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:17.130
Luckily, we were able to get
the interior quite clean,

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:20.040
so this won't have to be repigmented.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.470
Now we're going to apply our topcoat.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:26.310
For this particular bag,
I chose a matte topcoat.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:30.300
And this actually will
lock in all the pigment

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.546
that we previously put on.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:39.356
I am super excited

00:06:39.356 --> 00:06:41.372
with how this restoration turned out,

00:06:41.372 --> 00:06:45.237
and I'm so excited to see
how the client likes it

00:06:45.237 --> 00:06:47.437
when she receives her bag.

